From b524d43eab12fb57ea3192acfad644f7901358df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:34:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/112] model + moe-stream : SiegeLadder G44 - G35's lens
 with a learned correction (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G44=<gguf file>, off by default).
 For each pair S -> S + 2 a ridge regression (strength 0.1 x the mean of the
 Gram matrix's diagonal; C17's dumps, 98 sequences, 199K tokens of router
 inputs) of the target router's logits z_T(x_T) - z_T(x_S) over S's router
 input x_S, folded into the target's router: the lens multiplies x_S by W'_S =
 G_{S+2} + B_S^T (f16 [5120, 384]) instead of G_{S+2} - the same GEMV with
 another matrix, nothing more computed. 38 matrices (1017 has no hash layers),
 142.5 MiB in a buffer of the expert caches' device
 (llama_moe_stream::load_g44 after alloc_bufs; the file's g44.depth must match
 G35's depth, and without G35 or next to runahead it stays unloaded). G35's
 read-ahead and G40's staging both take it. Offline on held-out sequences:
 top-6 agreement at d = 2 0.617 -> 0.713, better on every one of the 38 pairs;
 in the tier model 12% fewer calls waiting on the drive and 31% fewer drive
 reads. In the fork (og default, teacher forcing without C7, GPU scheduling
 off, A B B A): -1.12 ms a token (+2.0%; +2.3% at zero drive stalls), drive
 wait 8.63 -> 7.71 ms, drive reads 95 -> 73 slabs a token, drops -0.9%; G40 k
 1 stages with precision 0.90 against 0.77 (a third of the wrong stagings),
 G40 k 1 + G44 +8.6% over the default against +5.4% for G40 alone. The math is
 untouched - only when experts are read: with the drop rule off the logits
 match the arm without it to the rounding of the stored base (mean KLD 0 +-
 1e-6, top-1 100%, PPL per chunk equal) (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.266 / 4.270;
 the file: bench/g44_fit2.py export)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
